**W3 — Create a doctrine** (FR-9, FR-12)

```
$ lore doctrine new tdd-feature-lite --group default -d /tmp/design.md -m /tmp/recon.md /tmp/feature-spec.md /tmp/scribe.md
Created doctrine tdd-feature-lite with 3 missions in group default
```

Exit 0. Ungrouped:

```
$ lore doctrine new tdd-feature-lite -d /tmp/design.md -m /tmp/recon.md
Created doctrine tdd-feature-lite with 1 mission
```

```
$ lore --json doctrine new tdd-feature-lite --group default -d /tmp/design.md -m /tmp/recon.md /tmp/feature-spec.md /tmp/scribe.md
{"created": "tdd-feature-lite", "group": "default", "missions": ["feature-spec", "recon", "scribe"], "path": ".lore/doctrines/default/tdd-feature-lite/"}
```

`group` is `null` and `path` is `.lore/doctrines/tdd-feature-lite/` when
`--group` is absent. `missions` is sorted by id.

Failures write nothing:

```
$ lore doctrine new tdd-feature-lite -d /tmp/design.md
At least one mission file is required (-m)
```

stderr, exit 1.

```
$ lore doctrine new tdd-feature-lite -m /tmp/recon.md
Error: -d/--design is required
```

stderr, exit 1.

```
$ lore doctrine new tdd-feature-lite -d /tmp/design.md -m /tmp/a/recon.md /tmp/b/recon.md
Duplicate mission id "recon": two -m files share a filename stem
```

stderr, exit 1.

---

**W4 — Edit a doctrine** (FR-10, FR-11, FR-12)

```
$ lore doctrine edit tdd-feature-lite -m /tmp/recon.md
Updated doctrine tdd-feature-lite (missions replaced: recon)
```

```
$ lore doctrine edit tdd-feature-lite -d /tmp/design.md
Updated doctrine tdd-feature-lite (design replaced)
```

```
$ lore doctrine edit tdd-feature-lite --remove-mission refactor lint
Updated doctrine tdd-feature-lite (missions removed: lint, refactor)
```

```
$ lore doctrine edit tdd-feature-lite -d /tmp/d.md -m /tmp/recon.md --remove-mission lint
Updated doctrine tdd-feature-lite (design replaced; missions replaced: recon; missions removed: lint)
```

All exit 0. Clause order is fixed: design, replaced, removed. Clauses are joined
with `; `. Each list is sorted by id and joined with `, `.

```
$ lore --json doctrine edit tdd-feature-lite -m /tmp/recon.md
{"updated": "tdd-feature-lite", "design_replaced": false, "missions_replaced": ["recon"], "missions_removed": []}
```

Failures, all exit 1 with nothing written:

```
$ lore doctrine edit tdd-feature-lite
Nothing to update: pass -d, -m, or --remove-mission
```

See **Conflict C-2** — the PRD calls this a usage error and specifies exit 1,
while `conceptual-workflows-error-handling` and the sibling `lore edit` command
make a usage error exit 2 through `click.UsageError`.

```
$ lore doctrine edit tdd-feature-lite --remove-mission lint
Mission "lint" not found in doctrine "tdd-feature-lite"
```

```
$ lore doctrine edit tdd-feature-lite --remove-mission recon
Cannot remove every mission: a doctrine keeps at least one mission.
```

```
$ lore doctrine edit nope -m /tmp/recon.md
Doctrine "nope" not found.
```

Field-edit mode is unchanged in shape and now targets the design document
(R19a):

```
$ lore doctrine edit tdd-feature-lite --set title="TDD Feature Lite v2"
Updated doctrine tdd-feature-lite
```

Exit 0. `--set/--unset/--add/--remove` stay mutually exclusive with `-d`, `-m`
and `--remove-mission`.

