**W5 — Assign a doctrine mission to a Lore mission** (FR-13)

```
$ lore new mission -q q-a1b2 "Map the codex and the binding decisions" -D tdd-feature-lite/recon -T agent -p 1 -d "<feature context>"
Created mission q-a1b2/m-c3d4
```

Exit 0, output unchanged from today. The reference is stored verbatim and is not
resolved or validated at write time.

```
$ lore edit q-a1b2/m-c3d4 -D tdd-feature-lite/feature-spec
Updated mission q-a1b2/m-c3d4
```

```
$ lore edit q-a1b2/m-c3d4 --no-doctrine-mission
Updated mission q-a1b2/m-c3d4
```

```
$ lore edit q-a1b2/m-c3d4 -D x/y --no-doctrine-mission
Error: --doctrine-mission and --no-doctrine-mission are mutually exclusive.
```

stderr, exit 2 — Click's `UsageError`, exactly as `--knight`/`--no-knight` is
today.

---

**W6 — Receive a mission as a worker** (FR-14, FR-15)

```
$ lore show q-a1b2/m-c3d4
Mission: q-a1b2/m-c3d4
Title: Map the codex and the binding decisions
Status: in_progress
Priority: 1
Type: agent
Description: <feature context>
Doctrine Mission: tdd-feature-lite/recon
Created: 2026-09-15T19:27:21Z
Updated: 2026-09-15T20:36:54Z

Board:
  [2026-09-15T20:34:47Z] PRD: doctrine-missions-prd

--- Mission Instructions ---
# Recon

You are Recon. You map the ground before anyone builds on it.
```

Exit 0. The body is printed verbatim with no trailing newline added and **no
re-rendered frontmatter block** — this differs from today's
`--- Knight Contents ---`, which re-rendered `id`/`title`/`summary` above the
body.

Unresolvable reference:

```
$ lore show q-a1b2/m-c3d4
Mission: q-a1b2/m-c3d4
Title: Map the codex and the binding decisions
Status: in_progress
Priority: 1
Type: agent
Doctrine Mission: gone/missing
Created: 2026-09-15T19:27:21Z
Updated: 2026-09-15T20:36:54Z
```

Exit 0, **silent** — no `Warning:` line. This deletes the
`Warning: knight file "..." not found in .lore/knights/` line that exists today.
See Draft ADR 5.

```
$ lore show q-a1b2/m-c3d4 --json
{"id": "q-a1b2/m-c3d4", ..., "mission_type": "agent", "doctrine_mission": "tdd-feature-lite/recon", "doctrine_mission_contents": "# Recon\n\nYou are Recon...\n", ...}
```

`knight` and `knight_contents` no longer exist as keys.
`doctrine_mission_contents` is `null` when the reference does not resolve and
when `--no-doctrine-mission` is passed.

