**W7 — Audit a project after upgrading** (FR-21, FR-22)

```
$ lore health --scope doctrines
WARNING  doctrines  tdd-feature  missing_missions_dir: no missions/ directory — this doctrine is not readable in the current shape
WARNING  doctrines  tdd-feature  stray_yaml: tdd-feature.yaml is no longer read
Health check passed. No issues found.
```

The last line is not printed when issues exist; it is shown here only to name
the renderer. The real no-issue output is that line alone. Exit **0** — warnings
never raise the exit code.

```
$ lore health --scope doctrines
ERROR  doctrines  tdd-feature-lite/recon  missing_file: referenced by q-a1b2/m-c3d4 but not found on disk
```

Exit 1.

```
$ lore health --scope knights
Usage: lore health [OPTIONS] [EXTRA_SCOPES]...
Try 'lore health --help' for help.

Error: Invalid value for '--scope': 'knights' is not one of 'codex', 'artifacts', 'doctrines', 'watchers', 'schemas', 'glossary', 'bindings', 'rites', 'voice', 'skills'.
```

stderr, exit 2 — Click's own wording, produced by dropping the token from the
`click.Choice` set (ADR-017).

> The PRD renders these health lines without the severity prefix and with a
> space instead of `: ` before the detail. That is the PRD describing the check
> name, severity and detail; the rendering above is what `cli.health_cmd`'s
> existing renderer actually emits and is not being changed. The normative
> content — severity, `entity_type`, `id`, `check`, `detail` — is exactly what
> the PRD specifies.

