#### Added by the ADR & Standards Audit — documents the table above omitted

`grep -ril knight .lore/codex/` returns **88 files**, of which 6 are the transient
feature docs and 6 are the documents this table retires. The table above named
about half the remainder. These are the rest. Every one describes the Knight
entity, `knight.py`, `missions.knight` or `lore knight` as **current state**, so
`decisions-020-codex-voice-is-enforced` ("a canonical codex document carries what
is true now") makes each one a defect the moment the code lands. This is not the
pre-existing staleness the In Scope / Out of Scope section declines to repair —
it is staleness this feature creates.

**Two rows are mechanically enforced**, not stylistic: `_check_codex` emits
`broken_related_link` at **severity `error`** (`health.py:229-234`) for a
`related:` entry naming a document that does not exist. Retiring the six knight
documents without editing the fourteen documents whose frontmatter names them
makes `lore health` exit 1 on this repository — which is exactly what S7's
"`lore health` on this repository reports no new errors" gate measures, one lane
before the scribe runs.

