## Part 4 — Test Strategy

### Conventions

Unit tests live in `tests/unit/`, import `lore.*` modules directly, never
`lore.cli`, and use `bare_lore_dir` or `tree` from `tests/unit/conftest.py`.
E2E tests live in `tests/e2e/`, use the root `project_dir` and `runner`
fixtures, and cite one `conceptual-workflows-*` id in the module docstring. No
file defines its own `runner` or `project_dir`. No `US-N`, `AC-N` or
`SCENARIO-NNN` in any name, comment or docstring.

The anchoring rule is `technical-test-guidelines` §3, and the existing suite
breaches it widely — see C-3's corrected statement of the tree. Every E2E file
this feature **creates or rewrites** carries the anchor its E-table row names,
which repairs the anchor on `test_doctrine_show.py`, `test_doctrine_new.py` and
`test_doctrine_list.py` in passing. Files this feature only edits keep whatever
anchor they have. Repairing the suite-wide breach is not this feature's work,
and no file this feature touches may lose an anchor it already has.

Nothing is mocked around a failure path: a missing file is a missing file on
disk, a dangling reference is a real row pointing at a real absent path, and a
migration test opens a real v6 database. The one sanctioned mock in this area is
the existing `health.get_validator` monkeypatch anchor, which is unchanged.

`decisions-006-no-seed-content-tests` governs every assertion touching
`src/lore/defaults/`: existence, parseability and required-key presence only.
Never assert a seeded doctrine's title, a seeded mission's summary, the prose of
`mission-design.md`, or the text of a retirement reason. "The four seeded
doctrines each have a `missions/` directory containing at least one `.md` file
whose frontmatter parses and carries `id`, `title` and `summary`" is a valid
assertion; "the `recon` mission's title is `Map the codex`" is not.

CliRunner note: on Click 8.3 `mix_stderr=False` no longer exists; read
`result.stdout` and `result.stderr` separately.

### E2E

