---

## Part 5 — Implementation Plan

This section is the dispatch order. The orchestrator creates one mission per
in-scope lane, in this order, and each dev knight executes its own section end to
end.

> **Read this before dispatching.** This feature is a single coordinated
> breaking change, not three independent ones. The suite is green at the end of
> the **foundation** lane and again only at the end of the **surface** lane.
> From core unit C1 until the last surface unit the tree is red by construction:
> C1 changes `doctrine.py`'s return shape while `cli.py` still reads `raw_yaml`,
> and core's excision unit deletes `knight.py` while `api.py` still re-exports
> from it. Each unit below therefore carries a **Done when** that is runnable at
> that moment — a targeted test selection, an import check, or a `grep` — and
> never "the suite is green". The orchestrator must not read a red suite between
> C1 and S7 as a regression, and must not stop after core: core alone leaves
> `lore.api` unimportable.

### Lane: foundation

_In scope._ Purely additive. Ends with the full suite green.

| # | Unit | Files | Tests first | Done when |
|---|------|-------|-------------|-----------|
| F1 | Add the `doctrine-mission-frontmatter` schema and register the kind | `src/lore/schemas/doctrine-mission-frontmatter.yaml` (new), `src/lore/schemas/__init__.py` (`_FRONTMATTER_KINDS` gains the kind) | `tests/unit/test_schemas.py` — `load_schema("doctrine-mission-frontmatter")` returns `required == ["id","title","summary"]`; `validate_entity` reports a missing field and an unknown property with the standard messages | Those tests pass and `pytest tests/unit tests/e2e` is green — nothing else reads the new kind yet |
| F2 | Add the doctrine path helpers | `src/lore/paths.py` — `DESIGN_SUFFIX`, `MISSIONS_DIRNAME`, `doctrine_design_path`, `doctrine_missions_dir`, `doctrine_mission_path`; module docstring notes that these take a doctrine directory | `tests/unit/test_paths.py` — each helper returns the expected path and creates nothing on disk | Those tests pass; `knights_dir` is **still present** (it leaves in C4); full suite green |
| F3 | Correct the design-frontmatter schema description | `src/lore/schemas/doctrine-design-frontmatter.yaml` — `id`'s description becomes "Doctrine id. Must match the doctrine directory name."; required set unchanged | `tests/unit/test_schemas.py` — the required set is still `["id","title","summary"]` | That test passes; full suite green |

### Lane: core

_In scope._ The largest lane. Everything under `src/lore/` except `api.py`,
`cli.py` and `prompts.py`, plus the test-suite excision.

| # | Unit | Files | Tests first | Done when |
|---|------|-------|-------------|-----------|
| C1 | Rewrite `doctrine.py` for the directory model | `src/lore/doctrine.py` (wholesale), `tests/unit/conftest.py` (`NestedTree.doctrine` writes the new shape) | `tests/unit/test_doctrine.py`, `test_doctrine_crud.py`, `test_doctrine_crud_holistic.py`, `test_doctrine_valueerror.py` — rewritten first, covering every `lore.doctrine.*` row of the Unit table: discovery and the skip rule, `read_doctrine`'s two miss shapes, the ten-step create validation order with each exact message, merge-by-stem, soft-delete, the last-mission guard, the staged write leaving nothing behind on failure, and both resolvers including the traversal refusals | `pytest tests/unit/test_doctrine.py tests/unit/test_doctrine_crud.py tests/unit/test_doctrine_crud_holistic.py tests/unit/test_doctrine_valueerror.py` is green; `grep -n "steps\|cycle\|_normalize\|raw_yaml" src/lore/doctrine.py` returns nothing |
| C2 | Rename the column end to end and migrate | `src/lore/models.py`, `src/lore/db.py`, `src/lore/migrations/v6_to_v7.py` (new), `src/lore/defaults/schema.sql`, `src/lore/oracle.py`, `tests/conftest.py` (`insert_mission`) | `tests/unit/test_models.py`, `test_db_mission_detail.py`, `test_db_edit_full.py`, `test_db_mission_crud_holistic.py`, `test_db_list_missions_grouped.py`, `test_db_quest_detail.py` — rewritten for `doctrine_mission`, the two `remove_*` precedence cases, and hydration through `_resolve_doctrine_mission` including the traversal refusal | `pytest tests/unit/test_models.py tests/unit/test_db_*.py` is green; `sqlite3` on a hand-built v6 file reports version 7 with the new column and no `knight`; `grep -n "knight" src/lore/db.py src/lore/models.py src/lore/oracle.py` returns nothing |
| C3 | Rework the health doctrines scope | `src/lore/health.py` — `_check_doctrines` rewritten to the eight rows, `_check_knights` and `_is_knight_soft_deleted` deleted, `knights` dropped from `_ALL_SCOPES` and the `checkers` map, `_SCHEMA_KINDS` and `_FRONTMATTER_SCHEMA_KINDS` updated | `tests/unit/test_health.py`, `test_health_schemas.py`, `test_health_schemas_us007.py` — rewritten for every row of the health table, the closed-mission and soft-delete suppressions, the one-row-per-reference grouping, and the ten-scope `ValueError` message | `pytest tests/unit/test_health.py tests/unit/test_health_schemas*.py` is green; `grep -n "knight" src/lore/health.py` returns nothing |
| C4 | Excise the Knight entity from the code | `src/lore/knight.py` (deleted), `src/lore/schemas/knight-frontmatter.yaml` (deleted), `src/lore/schemas/doctrine-yaml.yaml` (deleted), `src/lore/schemas/__init__.py`, `src/lore/paths.py` (`knights_dir` and the `"knight"` row deleted), `src/lore/frontmatter_edit.py` (`knight` kind and import deleted, `doctrine` kind repointed, `_doctrine_design_locator` added), `src/lore/api.py` (the five knight callable re-exports, `_knight`, `_validate_frontmatter`, and `Knight`/`Doctrine`/`DoctrineStep` from the `lore.models` import at `api.py:15` — **only** these lines; see D26. `__all__` itself is S1's, but the `models` import line is C4's, because C2 already deleted the three dataclasses and `import lore.api` raises `ImportError` until this lands) | `tests/unit/test_paths.py`, `test_paths_entity_location.py`, `test_schemas.py`, `test_frontmatter_edit.py`, `test_frontmatter_edit_overlay.py` — rewritten for the removed kinds, the `entity_location` `ValueError` message, and the repointed `doctrine` kind editing the design file's frontmatter with a byte-identical body | `python -c "import lore.api"` succeeds; `grep -rn "knight" src/lore/ --include='*.py'` returns only `cli.py` and `prompts.py`; `pytest tests/unit/test_paths.py tests/unit/test_paths_entity_location.py tests/unit/test_schemas.py tests/unit/test_frontmatter_edit*.py` is green |
| C5 | Stop seeding knights and remove the retired tree | `src/lore/init.py` (`SEEDED_TREES` loses the `knights` row; `RETIRED_SEED_TREES` added with its walk, its report lines and the authored-knights notice; the `for package in (...)` loop updated), `src/lore/defaults/gitignore` (three lines removed), `src/lore/defaults/knights/**` (12 files deleted) | `tests/unit/test_lore_init.py`, `test_reconcile.py`, `test_initplan.py` — the retired-tree walk unlinks files, skips symlinks, survives an unlinkable file, prunes emptied directories and produces one message per removal; `seeded_paths()` names no knight path; a project with no `.lore/knights/` produces no messages | `pytest tests/unit/test_lore_init.py tests/unit/test_reconcile.py tests/unit/test_initplan.py` is green; `find src/lore/defaults/knights` reports no such path; `grep -n knights src/lore/defaults/gitignore` returns nothing |
| C6 | Excise Knight from the test suite's shared surface | `tests/e2e/test_knight_list.py`, `test_knight_crud.py`, `test_api_parity_knight.py`, `test_health_grouped_knight_refs.py`, `tests/unit/test_knight_crud.py`, `test_knight.py`, `test_knight_crud_holistic.py`, `test_health_grouped_knight_refs.py` (all deleted); `tests/unit/conftest.py` (`bare_lore_dir`, `_ENTITY_DIRS`, `NestedTree.entity`) | None — this unit removes tests and fixtures | The eight files are gone; `grep -rn "knight" tests/conftest.py tests/unit/conftest.py tests/e2e/conftest.py` returns nothing; `pytest --collect-only tests/` completes without a collection error |

### Lane: surface

_In scope._ `api.py`, `cli.py`, `prompts.py`, and the E2E suite. Ends with the
full suite green — this lane is what closes the red window.

| # | Unit | Files | Tests first | Done when |
|---|------|-------|-------------|-----------|
| S1 | Finish `api.py` | `src/lore/api.py` — `__all__` updated (**eight** names removed: `list_knights`, `read_knight`, `create_knight`, `update_knight`, `delete_knight`, `Knight`, `Doctrine`, `DoctrineStep`; grouped order otherwise preserved); the doctrine block's comment updated | `tests/unit/test_api_surface.py`, `test_api_all_matches_spec.py` — the literal `__all__` tuple edited to match, asserted element-for-element including order; `tests/e2e/test_python_api.py` — no knight name is reachable and neither `Doctrine` nor `DoctrineStep` is | `pytest tests/unit/test_api_surface.py tests/unit/test_api_all_matches_spec.py` is green; `python -c "from lore.api import *"` raises nothing |
| S2 | Delete the `lore knight` command group and every knight touchpoint in `cli.py` | `src/lore/cli.py` — the five `knight_*` commands and the `knight` group (≈360 lines), `from lore.api import _knight as knight_module`, the two `_PROJECT_READ_COMMANDS` entries, `"knights"` in `_VALID_SCOPES`, the `Knight` line in the top-level help, the knight sentences in the `lore init` help paragraph | `tests/e2e/test_error_handling.py` — `lore knight list` exits 2 with `No such command 'knight'.`; `tests/e2e/test_health.py` — `--scope knights` exits 2; `tests/unit/test_cli_imports_only_api.py`, `test_cli_health.py`, `test_help_enrichment.py` | `grep -rn "knight" src/lore/cli.py` returns nothing; those tests pass |
| S3 | Rewrite `lore doctrine show` | `src/lore/cli.py` — `doctrine_show` gains `--mission`, prints design + index, wraps both JSON envelopes, routes JSON errors to stderr on both flag paths | `tests/e2e/test_doctrine_show.py` rewritten first — E1–E8 | `pytest tests/e2e/test_doctrine_show.py` is green |
| S4 | Rewrite `lore doctrine new` | `src/lore/cli.py` — `-d` required, `-m` as `SpaceSeparatedChoice`, `load_mission_sources`, the new message and envelope; the `-f/--from` flag removed | `tests/e2e/test_doctrine_new.py` rewritten first — E9–E16 | `pytest tests/e2e/test_doctrine_new.py` is green |
